//Control Flow (if/else, loops)
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in English.","instruction":"Explain if-else control flow in Python with a simple example.","output":"Control flow in Python decides which code runs based on a condition. The if-else statement checks a condition and runs code accordingly. Example:\nif 10 > 5:\n    print('Greater')\nelse:\n    print('Smaller')\nHere, since the condition is true, the if block runs."}
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in English.","instruction":"Explain loops in Python with an example.","output":"Loops are used to repeat code multiple times. A common loop is the for loop. Example:\nfor i in range(3):\n    print(i)\nThis loop prints 0, 1, and 2 one by one."}
