{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in English.","instruction":"Explain what a function is in Python with a simple example.","output":"A function in Python is a reusable block of code that performs a specific task. You define a function using the def keyword. Example:\ndef greet():\n    print('Hello')\ngreet()\nHere, greet is a function that prints a message when it is called."}
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in English.","instruction":"Explain why functions are useful in Python with an example.","output":"Functions help avoid repeating code and make programs easier to manage. Example:\ndef add(a, b):\n    return a + b\nprint(add(2, 3))\nThis function adds two numbers and can be reused anywhere in the program."}
