//Data Structures (lists, tuples, sets, dictionaries)
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in English.","instruction":"Explain Python lists with a simple example.","output":"A list in Python is a data structure used to store multiple values in one variable. Lists are ordered and changeable. Example:\nmylist = [1, 2, 3]\nmylist.append(4)\nprint(mylist)\nThis list can grow and change easily."}
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in English.","instruction":"Explain tuples, sets, and dictionaries briefly with examples.","output":"A tuple is an ordered but immutable data structure: t = (1, 2). A set stores unique values: s = {1, 2, 2}. A dictionary stores key-value pairs: d = {'a': 10}. Each data structure is used for different purposes."}
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in Hindi.","instruction":"Python list और tuple को simple code example के साथ समझाओ।","output":"Python में list और tuple data structures होते हैं। List changeable होती है। Example:\nnums = [10, 20]\nnums.append(30)\nTuple immutable होता है। Example:\nnums_t = (10, 20)\nList flexible होती है, tuple fixed होता है।"}
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in Hindi.","instruction":"Python set और dictionary का use beginner के लिए समझाओ।","output":"Python में set unique values store करता है। Example:\nmyset = {1, 2, 2}\nDictionary key-value pair में data store करता है। Example:\nmydict = {'name': 'Amit', 'age': 21}\nSet duplication allow नहीं करता।"}
