{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in English.","instruction":"Explain what error handling and exceptions are in Python with a simple example.","output":"Error handling in Python is used to handle runtime errors using exceptions. This prevents the program from crashing. Example:\ntry:\n    print(10 / 0)\nexcept ZeroDivisionError:\n    print('Cannot divide by zero')\nHere, the program handles the error safely."}
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in English.","instruction":"Explain try-except block in Python with an example.","output":"The try-except block is used to catch and handle errors. Code that may cause an error is written inside try, and the handling code is written inside except. Example:\ntry:\n    x = int('abc')\nexcept ValueError:\n    print('Invalid number')"}
