//Object-Oriented Programming (classes, inheritance, polymorphism)
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in English.","instruction":"Explain what Object-Oriented Programming is in Python with a simple example.","output":"Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) in Python is a way of writing code using classes and objects. A class is like a blueprint. Example:\nclass Student:\n    def greet(self):\n        print('Hello')\ns = Student()\ns.greet()\nHere, Student is a class and s is an object of that class."}
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in English.","instruction":"Explain inheritance and polymorphism in Python with a simple example.","output":"Inheritance allows one class to use properties of another class. Polymorphism allows the same method name to behave differently. Example:\nclass Animal:\n    def sound(self):\n        print('Animal sound')\nclass Dog(Animal):\n    def sound(self):\n        print('Bark')\nDog().sound()\nHere, Dog inherits Animal and overrides the sound method."}
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in Hindi.","instruction":"Python में Object-Oriented Programming क्या है? Simple example के साथ समझाओ।","output":"Python में Object-Oriented Programming का मतलब है classes और objects का उपयोग करके program लिखना। Class एक blueprint होती है। Example:\nclass Car:\n    def start(self):\n        print('Car started')\nc = Car()\nc.start()\nयहाँ Car एक class है और c उसका object है।"}
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in Hindi.","instruction":"Python में inheritance और polymorphism को आसान शब्दों में समझाओ।","output":"Python में inheritance का मतलब है एक class का दूसरी class से properties लेना। Polymorphism का मतलब है same function name का अलग behavior होना। Example:\nclass Shape:\n    def draw(self):\n        print('Drawing shape')\nclass Circle(Shape):\n    def draw(self):\n        print('Drawing circle')\nयहाँ Circle class, Shape से inherit करती है।"}
