//Testing & Debugging (unit tests, pytest, logging)
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in English.","instruction":"Explain testing and debugging in Python with a simple example.","output":"Testing and debugging help ensure your code works correctly. Testing checks expected behavior, while debugging finds and fixes errors. Example of a simple test:\ndef add(a, b):\n    return a + b\nassert add(2, 3) == 5\nIf the assertion passes, the function works as expected."}
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in English.","instruction":"Explain unit testing and pytest briefly with an example.","output":"Unit testing tests small parts of code like functions. pytest is a popular testing framework. Example:\ndef add(a, b):\n    return a + b\n\ndef test_add():\n    assert add(1, 2) == 3\nRunning pytest will automatically execute this test."}
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in Hindi.","instruction":"Python में testing और debugging क्या होते हैं? Simple example के साथ समझाओ।","output":"Python में testing का मतलब है code सही काम कर रहा है या नहीं यह check करना। Debugging का मतलब है error ढूंढकर उसे fix करना। Example:\ndef div(a, b):\n    return a / b\nअगर error आए तो debugging से problem समझी जाती है।"}
