//Concurrency (multithreading, multiprocessing, async/await)
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in English.","instruction":"Explain what concurrency is in Python with a simple example.","output":"Concurrency in Python means running multiple tasks at the same time. This helps improve performance for tasks like waiting for input/output. Example using threading:\nimport threading\n\ndef task():\n    print('Task running')\n\nt = threading.Thread(target=task)\nt.start()\nThis runs the task concurrently."}
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in English.","instruction":"Explain async and await in Python with an example.","output":"async and await are used for asynchronous programming in Python. They help handle I/O-bound tasks efficiently. Example:\nimport asyncio\n\nasync def main():\n    print('Hello')\n\nasyncio.run(main())\nThis runs code asynchronously without blocking."}
{"system":"You are a Python Tutor. Explain in Hindi.","instruction":"Python में multithreading और multiprocessing को आसान शब्दों में समझाओ।","output":"Python में multithreading और multiprocessing concurrency के तरीके हैं। Multithreading एक process में multiple threads चलाता है, और multiprocessing multiple processes चलाता है। Example:\nimport multiprocessing\nprint('Process started')\nये heavy tasks के लिए useful होता है।"}
